e", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Dana Lee's flight and hotel are both booked and confirmed, with one reservation for each and nothing charged twice.\n\n**What's booked:**\n- **Flight R0001:** F100, nonstop from SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, **$289**. This was the cheapest nonstop. F120 was cheaper at $199 but has a stop.\n- **Hotel R0002:** Midtown Lodge (H1), New York, checking in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night, **$378 total**. This was the cheapest hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total charged to the corporate card: $667.** That's under the $1000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\n**What went wrong:** I tried to book both together with `book_trip`, but the request timed out. I retried with the same request ID, which stops the system from running it twice. That showed the original request had partly failed: the flight was booked but the hotel step hit an internal error. So I booked the hotel on its own with `book_hotel`.\n\nAs a result, the flight and hotel are separate reservations rather than one combined trip.", "type": "text"}]}]}